{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190186": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Non-Tenure-Track, Department of Biology",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Arts and Sciences: Arts and Sciences - Sciences: Biology Location: Baylor University, Waco, TX The Department of Biology ( www.baylor.edu/biology ) in the College of Arts & Sciences ( www.baylor.edu/artsandsciences ) seeks applications for a non-tenure-track, full-time Assistant Teaching Professor faculty position starting in August 2027. We welcome candidates from all fields of biology, as our curriculum offers diverse teaching opportunities, from foundational courses such as Modern Concepts in Bioscience and Genetics to advanced topics such as Ecology and Molecular Genomics. This position may include responsibilities for laboratory curriculum and management; thus, we are interested in instructors with some experience in undergraduate laboratories. Laboratory responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, oversight of the introductory biology laboratory courses and the Graduate Teaching Assistants (GTAs) who support them. Assistant Teaching Professors are expected to use educational strategies that emphasize student-centered learning and enable transformative learning experiences in lecture and laboratory courses. Experience or interest in innovative curricula for lab courses that foster a culture of discovery will be viewed as a strength. The department currently supports several course-based undergraduate research experiences (CUREs) and promotes an undergraduate Learning Assistant program to enhance active learning in our lectures and labs. This position is a 9-month appointment during the academic year. The appointment is a renewable, full-time, benefits-eligible, teaching and laboratory oversight position with a promotion pathway to Associate Teaching Professor and Teaching Professor. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other non-immigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Successful candidates will hold a Ph.D. or equivalent in a biologically related discipline. A track record of developing student-centered learning activities is expected. Previous teaching experience is preferred but not required. Successful candidates will be able to contribute to one or more of the following: course development, training, and oversight of Graduate Teaching Assistants (GTA), contributing to the department’s Learning Assistants (LA) program, mentoring undergraduate students, and supervising student teaching labs. Applications will be accepted starting August 10, 2026.  Completed applications must be received by 11pm Central time on December 1, 2026 . To apply, please submit the following materials electronically via Interfolio: A cover letter of application, A 1-2 page teaching statement, A curriculum vitae A transcript from the highest-degree granting institution (unofficial copy acceptable for application. If the Ph.D. is in progress, a copy of the transcript of completed Ph.D. hours should also be submitted), and The contact information for three individuals the search committee can contact for letters of recommendation. Selected applicants will be contacted to complete a required, self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form. Candidates invited for an on-campus interview must provide official transcripts at that time. Questions concerning the position can be sent to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Jon Lawson at jonathan_lawson@baylor.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187222": {
      "title": "Robert and Veronica K. Piziak Endowed Chair in Mathematics",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Arts and Sciences: Arts and Sciences - Sciences: Mathematics Location: Waco, Texas The Department of Mathematics in the College of Arts & Sciences at Baylor University invites applications for the Robert and Veronica K. Piziak Endowed Chair in Mathematics , a tenured position at the rank of Professor beginning August 2027. We seek an internationally recognized scholar with a vibrant research program in mathematics. The ideal candidate will have exceptional expertise and a record of research at the forefront of important advances in the field. The successful candidate will be expected to make significant contributions to the department’s research and teaching missions. We seek a collegial faculty member who will contribute positively to a departmental culture of outstanding research, excellent teaching, and dedicated service to undergraduate and graduate students. Review of completed applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled or February 1, 2027, whichever comes first. For details about the position and to apply, see apply.interfolio.com/187222. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. I t has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Candidates must possess a doctoral degree in mathematics or a closely related field. Applicants are expected to have a distinguished record of publication and scholarship in mathematics. Experience securing external grant funding and mentoring graduate students is preferred. A complete application must include the following materials submitted electronically via Interfolio at apply.interfolio.com/187222: • A cover letter. • A curriculum vitae. • The names, institutional affiliations, and email addresses of three references. • An unofficial doctoral transcript. Official transcripts will be required for candidates invited for a campus interview. • The self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Fritz Gesztesy, Search Committee Chair, at fritz_gesztesy@baylor.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186519": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Non-Tenure-Track, American Politics, Department of Political Science",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Arts and Sciences: Arts and Sciences - Humanities and Social Sciences: Political Science Location: Waco, Texas The Department of Political Science at Baylor University seeks a full-time, Assistant Teaching Professor in American Politics to begin August 2027. The primary teaching responsibility will be teaching PSC 1387: The U.S. Constitution, Its Interpretation, and the American Political Experience , a general education course required of nearly all undergraduates. Additionally, the candidate may have the opportunity to develop other American politics courses. The ability to develop other introductory courses in a second subfield would be welcome, but not expected. Assistant Teaching Professor appointments are renewable full-time, benefits-eligible, teaching-focused positions with six-year promotion paths to Associate Teaching Professor for successful candidates and twelve-year promotion paths to Teaching Professor for highly successful candidates. Complete applications must be submitted by 11pm Central Time on November 15, 2026 . Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University : Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. I t has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing fauclty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Candidate must have a Ph.D. in political science or a related field by the time of appointment. Teaching experience is preferred. To apply, candidates should submit: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Statement of teaching philosophy 4. Teaching portfolio (including student evaluations and sample syllabi, if available) 5. Three letters of recommendation 6. Transcript from highest degree granting institution (unofficial copy acceptable) 7. Completed self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form (found in Interfolio) If you have questions about the position, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Dave Bridge ( David_Bridge@baylor.edu )."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190268": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor, Non-Tenure-Track, Accounting and Business Law",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Business: BUS Buffer: Accounting and Business Law Location: Waco, Texas The Department of Accounting and Business Law at the Hankamer School of Business, Baylor University, invites applications for a non-tenure-track Assistant Teaching Professor or Clinical Assistant Professor position starting in August 2027. The appointment as an Assistant Teaching Professor or Clinical Assistant Professor will depend on a candidate’s experience and qualifications. Baylor is a Christian research university with a rich tradition of teaching excellence. We invite candidates from diverse backgrounds who will help the department train undergraduate and graduate students in ways that model the Christian faith. An ideal candidate would have relevant professional and/or academic experience enabling them to teach a variety of accounting classes at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, with a strong preference for someone who can teach accounting information systems and/or emerging technology. Overall, applicants will be expected to commit to excellence in teaching and service and, in carrying out these responsibilities, commit to authentically living out their faith. ·       The position requires a graduate degree in accounting or a related field. ·       The ideal candidate will have either a PhD or a minimum of three years of professional experience. ·       An ideal candidate will have relevant professional and/or academic experience enabling them to teach a variety of accounting classes at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, with a strong preference for someone who can teach accounting information systems and/or emerging technology. ·       The applicant should be able to demonstrate their commitment to high-quality teaching and innovative and inclusive education. The Department of Accounting and Business Law: Accounting and Business Law, one of seven departments in the Hankamer School of Business, has a strong tradition of educating professionals who achieve positions of leadership in international organizations. The Department is AACSB-accredited and offers three degrees – BBA, Master of Accountancy (MAcc), and Master of Taxation (MTax). The flagship program is an integrated five-year curriculum that culminates in either the MAcc or MTax degree. With the current trends in our discipline, the department incorporates data analytics and emerging technology throughout the curriculum, and graduate students can earn a Certificate in Accounting Data and Analytics while completing coursework. The department has 28 accounting faculty members, approximately 400 undergraduate majors and 125 graduate students. For more information see www.baylor.edu/business/accounting/ . About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Review of applicants will begin on November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received after March 31, 2027, will not be considered. Interested individuals should apply via Interfolio. You will be requested to provide: 1)     A cover letter that highlights any relevant professional experience and credentials, interest in higher education instruction, and personal commitment to Baylor’s unique mission; 2)     A current Curriculum Vitae (CV); 3)     A transcript (either official or unofficial) of the highest degree earned or in progress; 4)     A statement of teaching describing how the applicant’s professional or academic experience shapes their teaching philosophy, approach to student engagement and mentoring, and vision for fostering effective and inclusive learning; and 5)     Contact information for three professional references. All applicants will also complete the self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form in Interfolio. For questions regarding the position, please contact either Cari Edison (cari_edison@baylor.edu) or Gia Chevis (gia_chevis@baylor.edu), search committee co-chairs.  For questions regarding the application process, please contact Marion Palomino, Office Manager ( Marion_Palomino@baylor.edu , 254.710.6465)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191739": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, non-tenure track, Finance",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Business: BUS Buffer: Finance, Insurance and Real Estate Location: Waco The Department of Finance in Baylor University's Hankamer School of Business invites applications for two full-time, non-tenure-track Assistant Teaching Professor of Finance beginning August 16, 2027. The position carries a 4/4 teaching load , together with service responsibilities. Primary responsibilities include: Teaching undergraduate Finance courses, potentiallly including upper-level courses consistent with departmental needs depending on qualifications Providing high-quality, student-centered instruction and contributing to continuous improvement in the Finance curriculum Mentoring students and supporting their academic and professional development Contributing to curriculum and program development Participating collegially in the service activities of the Department, Hankamer School of Business, and University The Department of Finance, Hankamer School of Business, and Baylor University provide strong support for effective teaching and student engagement. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits, allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination, Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds, guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. A master's or doctoral degree in Finance or a related field, completed or expected to be completed by August 2027 A record of, or strong potential for, effective teaching in undergraduate Finance courses Ability to teach a range of undergraduate Finance courses consistent with departmental needs Ability and willingness to mentor students and contribute to department, school, and university service Ability to support and contribute to Baylor University's Christian mission Applicants must submit the following materials through Interfolio: A one- to two-page cover letter describing the candidate's interest in the position, teaching qualifications, fit with the Department of Finance, and interest in supporting Baylor University's Christian mission Curriculum vitae A one- to two-page teaching statement describing the candidate's teaching philosophy, experience, effectiveness, ability to teach undergraduate Finance courses, and commitment to student mentoring An official or unofficial transcript for the highest degree earned or currently in progress One document containing the names and contact information of three professional references Applicants may submit additional materials demonstrating teaching effectiveness or relevant professional experience, including teaching evaluations or sample syllabi. All applicants must complete the self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form in Interfolio. Questions regarding the position or application process may be directed to Prof. David Dicks at David_Dicks@baylor.edu. For full consideration in the initial review, applications should be received by September 15, 2026 . Review will begin on September 16, 2026 , and will continue until the position is filled. Preliminary interviews will be conducted by Zoom, as appropriate to the search. Nothing received after April 15, 2027 , can be considered. Applicants whose qualifications and interests align with both this Assistant Teaching Professor of Finance position and the Clinical Assistant Professor of Finance position are welcome to apply to both searches. A separate application is required for each Interfolio posting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192440": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Sociology or Economics",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Honors: HON Buffer: Baylor Interdisciplinary Core Location: Waco, TX The Baylor Interdisciplinary Core (BIC) seeks a full-time Assistant Professor of Sociology or Economics (or related social science discipline.) Tenure-track Teaching and research expectations will follow Baylor's Faculty Workload Policy, found here . The preferred candidate will have expertise in Sociology or Economics who can address questions of markets, morality and economic systems with a primary-text curriculum, including but not limited to candidates with training in (1) economic sociology or anthropology (2) political economy, or (3) the history / theory of economics. The preferred candidate will have a research agenda capable of engaging audiences and questions beyond their home discipline, consistent with BIC's interdisciplinary mission. The preferred candidate is expected to contribute to interdisciplinary teaching across two of the following replacement core sequences in the BIC: World Cultures, Natural World, and Social World. Additional expectations for the position include: A willingness to collaborate in team teaching and mentoring undergraduate students. Collegial involvement in program, college and university events and service. Anticipated start date: August 2027 The Baylor Interdisciplinary Core is an integrated, team taught core curriculum program for Honors College students that emphasizes global and comparative perspective on primary texts in historical context. Emphasis on undergraduate education. Small seminar-style classes interspersed with large lectures. Canididates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. PhD or equivalent terminal degree in Sociology, Economics, or related discipline. The successful candidate will be expected to research and publish in their disciplinary/sub-disciplinary area and participate in program, college, and university service at levels appropriate to time served and/or rank. The anticipated start date is August 2027. Applicants should submit by November 1 st , 2026. All application materials must be submitted through Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/192440 A cover letter (Cover letters should describe candidates’ desire to join an interdisciplinary undergraduate department and match with Baylor's Mission ). An updated curriculum vitae. A two-page research statement. A two-page teaching philosophy statement. A list of three references. A Religious Affiliation Form (in Interfolio)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194853": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Teaching Fellow, Full Time Temporary Non Tenure-Track, Baylor Interdisciplinary Core",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Honors: HON Buffer: Baylor Interdisciplinary Core Location: Waco, TX The Baylor Interdisciplinary Core (BIC) is an integrated, team-taught core curriculum program for students in the Honors College that emphasizes global and comparative perspectives on primary texts in historical context. The BIC seeks to fill a full-time Postdoctoral Teaching Fellow position in the Honors College for the academic year s 2027-2028 and 2028–2029 , with an anticipated start date in August 2027. A third-year renewal of the appointment is possible. This is a full time temporary position and is neither tenure or tenure-track. We seek rising teacher-scholars working in Rhetoric and/or Composition or a related field with experience in writing instruction. The successful applicant must hold a doctoral degree or equivalent in relevant fields(awarded by August 21, 2027.) All applicants must complete the self-disclosed Religious Affliliation Form. Workload assignment is 75% teaching and 25% research.   Teaching typically involves  nine hours each semester. Course sequences in which fellows might teach include The Examined Life , World of Rhetoric , World Cultures , and Social World .  A full listing of BIC course sequences can be found here . During the period of their appointment, postdoctoral teaching fellows will receive mentored teaching and learning training, as well as research and publication workshops to support their faculty formation and prepare them for a position in higher education. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Graduated with PhD within 12 months preceding start date. Completed PhD within a timespan of five active years. Mission Fit with Baylor University All application materials should be submitted through the Intefolio link found here:  https://apply.interfolio.com/194853 A complete application consists of a (1) cover letter (2) curriculumvitae,and (3) list of three professional references. All applicants must complete the self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form. Cover letters should describe candidates’ research, approach to teaching, fit with the Baylor Interdisciplinary Core program, and fit with Baylor’s faith-based mission . Letters of recommendation from three professional references will be requested of selected candidates later in the review process. Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Initial interviews will occur over Zoom. Finalists will be invited for an in-person interview with the department, as well as college and university administration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192014": {
      "title": "Jim and Sharon Harrod Endowed Chair of Christian Thought",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Honors: HON Buffer: Honors Program Location: Waco, TX Baylor's Honors College seeks a full professor who will hold the Jim and Sharon Harrod Chair of Christian Thought. This is a full-time tenured position within the Honors Program, one of four departments within the Honors College. Applications from distinguished scholar-teachers within the humanities are sought. Anticipated start date is August 2027. Expectations Combining scholarly stature in the humanities, grasp of biblical and theological resources for integrating faith and learning, and the ability to inspire scholarly and general audiences, the Harrod Chair supports Baylor's mission of educating bright undergraduates for worldwide leadership and service by uniting academic excellence and Christian faith within a caring community. It is expected that the holder of this endowed chair will: Teach and mentor undergraduates studying within the Honors College by offering 4 three-credit-hour courses annually; Publish in leading academic journals and presses within his or her field; Pursue grant writing in support of research, public programs, or other initiatives that elevate Christian thought for the sake of morally purposeful and culturally enriched life; Address important figures, issues, and movements through books for general readership or articles in journals of public opinion, digital media, or newspaper opinion pages; Strengthen a distinguished honors curriculum through his or her professional contacts and relationships with thought leaders sympathetic to Christian faith and learning; Represent, through personal faith and practice, Christian intellectual life at its best. About the Honors College : The Honors College serves ~1,400 high-ability undergraduates through academic offerings that include a degree (B.Phil.), three interdisciplinary majors, an alternative core curriculum, and a traditional thesis-based honors program. Our students pursue 90+ majors across 8 other colleges and schools at Baylor. The HC features a 40-member regular full-time faculty that span anthropology, biology, classics, communication, comparative literature, creative writing, English, French, history, medicine, philosophy, political science, social psychology, and theology. Unique within American higher education, it unites the strengths of a highly regarded liberal arts college, an ascendant national research university, and an animating Christian mission. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. Nominations for this position may also be sent directly to the committee chair: Elizabeth_Corey@baylor.edu About Baylor University : Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Qualified applicants will possess: A Ph.D or equivalent terminal degree in a humanities field An academic record commensurate with appointment as a tenured full professor within the Honors College Evidence of high-quality classroom and seminar teaching of undergraduates and effective mentoring of students A history of multi- and interdisciplinary engagement that is grounded in disciplinary expertise and attuned to the integration of Christian faith and learning To apply, please submit the following materials via Interfolio: cover letter/letter of application C.V. transcript (unofficial or official) for highest degree earned contact information for three professional references Applicants will also complete the s elf-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form in Interfolio. Review of applicants will begin on November 15. Materials received after January 15 will not be considered."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187563": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Communication Sciences & Disorders,  Speech-Language Pathology",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Communication Sciences and Disorders Location: Baylor University, Waco Texas Anticipated Date of Appointment: August 2027 About the Position: The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders, within the Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences at Baylor University, invites applications and nominations for a full-time Tenure Track Faculty position in Speech-Language Pathology to join our dynamic and collaborative team. Primary expertise in medical speech-language pathology is preferred, particularly in pediatric feeding and swallowing or neurogenic communication disorders, including cognitive-communication disorders. Candidates with expertise in other areas of speech-language pathology, such as speech sound disorders, are also encouraged to apply. The position will include teaching and research responsibilities, with opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Baylor’s R1 research environment. Academic rank for this position will be at Assistant Professor level. Salary and Review Date Competitive salary support will be commensurate with experience. Application reviews will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To be fully considered, all application materials must be submitted by December 1, 2026 . About the Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders offers residential bachelor’s, residential and online master’s, and PhD degrees in Speech-Language Pathology; the program is CAA certified. Currently, the program is comprised of more than 300 undergraduate students, 75 residential graduate students, over 300 online graduate students, and twelve PhD students. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Required A Doctorate (Ph.D./Ed.D.) in Communication Sciences and Disorders, Speech and Hearing Sciences, or closely related field is required. Qualified candidates should have academic credentials commensurate with an appointment at the rank of assistant professor. The successful candidate will be expected to continue building upon a strong track record of interdisciplinary and collaborative research, scholarly productivity, and a demonstrated ability to secure extramural funding. In accordance with the university’s faith mission, to be considered, applicants must show evidence of an active Christian or Jewish faith. Preferred Primary expertise in pediatric feeding and swallowing or cognitive communication is preferred. Experience in teaching and/or research is preferred. Certification by ASHA (CCC-SLP) and eligibility for Texas State licensure are preferred. Special consideration will be given to candidates who demonstrate a strong foundation in research, publishing, and teaching excellence in communication sciences and disorders. Application Instructions A letter of application specifically addressing qualifications, research interests, and teaching philosophy; A curriculum vitae; Research Statement; Statement of Teaching Philosophy and Experience; An unofficial (or, preferably, official) transcript of the doctoral degree; and The contact information for three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. All applicants must complete the self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form in Interfolio. Inquiries regarding the position may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Douglas Petersen: douglas_petersen@baylor.edu . EEO/M/F/Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183963": {
      "title": "Lecturers, Part-time Temporary, Health, Human Performance and Recreation, FY26-27",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Health, Human Performance and Recreation Location: Waco, TX Part-time Lecturer positions for Health, Human Performance and Recreation Department, within Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences. These positions will teach courses in HHPR Dept. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as one of the top universities in the nation, achieving R1 institution status by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor also made it to the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education . It offers competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Candidates applying to teach Lifetime Fitness classes must have a Bachelor’s degree, and appropriate certifications (or life experiences in the area of expertise). A copy of courses offered are located on the Baylor HHPR website, https://hhpr.robbins.baylor.edu/ A master’s degree or required certification in a related field is needed to qualify for a part-time teaching position in other programs within HHPR Dept. A Cover letter and CV are required to be submitted via Interfolio. Also, all applicants must complete the self-disclosed Part-Time Mission Review."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184548": {
      "title": "Lecturers, Part-Time, Temporary, MAT Program FY 26-27",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Health, Human Performance and Recreation Location: Waco, TX Part-Time lecturer (adjunct) positions for the Master of Athletic Training Program in the Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences.  These positions will meet weekly with assigned student(s) to instruct and assess the students on associated clinical skills outlined in the Clinical Education course (HP 5110). About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as one of the top universities in the nation, achieving R1 institution status by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor also made it to the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education . It offers competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Masters degree in a related field, BOC certified, and state licensed as an athletic trainer Cover letter, C.V., copy of highest degree transcript and Part-Time Faculty Mission Review form should be submitted via Interfolio. Official transcript will be needed if hired."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191790": {
      "title": "Department Chair and Associate Professor or Professor, Tenured, Health, Human Performance and Recreation",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Health, Human Performance and Recreation Location: Waco, TX Baylor University seeks an experienced, collaborative, and innovative Associate Professor or Professor with tenure to serve as the Department Chair for the Department of Health, Human Performance and Recreation. The anticipated start date for this position is August 1, 2027. This is a full-time position. Details for this position can be found at apply.interfolio.com/191790 . The Department of Health, Human Performance and Recreation (HHPR) seeks a Department Chair to lead our growing department in meeting its mission of advancing the health sciences, kinesiology and recreation, and training the next generation of researchers and leaders in the varied disciplines within HHPR. The Chair will lead a department comprising faculty with a range of appointments and responsibilities, including tenured and tenure-track researchers, clinical faculty, and lecturers. The successful candidate will be committed to advancing research development, supporting excellence in teaching and professional practice, collaborating effectively with department and college-level leadership teams, and embodying a leadership approach that aligns with the University's strategic goals and Christian mission. Required: ·         A doctorate (e.g., Ph.D., Sc.D.) in health science, kinesiology, recreation, or a related field. ·         Credentials commensurate with an appointment at the rank of associate or full professor with tenure. ·         An active research agenda is expected with current or previous extramural funding. Preferred: ·         Previous academic leadership and administrative experience. ·         Experience mentoring and supporting the professional development of faculty. ·         A record of creative, collaborative, and practical solution-oriented leadership. ·         Evidence of the ability to lead, support, and advocate for a multidisciplinary academic department. ·         A record of effective teaching Candidates must submit all materials by October 1, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Applications will not be accepted after December 1, 2026. This search is being conducted using Interfolio’s Faculty Search Platform. Applicants must submit: (1)     Formal cover letter of application explicitly addressing qualifications and personal leadership philosophy. (2)     Current curriculum vitae. (3)     Official or unofficial transcript for highest degree. (4)     Contact information for three professional references. (5)     HHPR applicant information form. (6)     Self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form. Inquiries regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Elise King, at Elise_King@baylor.edu .  Application materials can be submitted at: apply.interfolio.com/191790 . Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Baylor University, a private not-for-profit university affiliated with the Baptist General Convention of Texas, is committed to compliance with all applicable anti-discrimination laws, including those regarding age, race, color, sex, national origin, military service, genetic information, and disability. Baylor complies with statutory Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity requirements. Baylor's full official Notice of Non-Discrimination may be read online."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192552": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Motor Learning/Motor Behavior,  Department of Health, Human Performance, and Recreation",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Health, Human Performance and Recreation Location: Waco, TX The Department of Health, Human Performance, and Recreation (HHPR) in the Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences at Baylor University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Motor Learning, Motor Control, Motor Behavior, or a related area of movement science beginning August 2027. This position will support the department's teaching, research, and service missions while contributing to the continued growth of Baylor University's nationally recognized research enterprise. We seek an innovative scholar whose research advances understanding of motor learning, motor control, motor behavior, skill acquisition, neuromotor function, rehabilitation, human performance, or similar related areas of movement sciences. Candidates who can establish interdisciplinary collaborations and contribute to Baylor University's growing research portfolio are especially encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to applicants whose work has translational relevance to the various dimensions of health, injury prevention, adapted physical activity and recreation, or clinical applications. The successful candidate will demonstrate expertise in motor learning and maintain a productive research agenda, pursue external funding, publish in high-quality peer-reviewed journals, and engage undergraduate and graduate students in meaningful research experiences. The candidate will also contribute to undergraduate and graduate motor learning teaching and related movement science courses. The successful candidate may also contribute to undergraduate instruction in adapted physical education or related program areas consistent with departmental needs and the candidate's expertise. About the Department & Facilities : HHPR faculty are engaged in cutting-edge research in human performance, neuromuscular function, exercise physiology, cellular muscle adaptation, biomechanics, and applied health sciences. Faculty collaborate across Baylor University with external partners including Baylor Scott & White Health and Baylor College of Medicine. The department values interdisciplinary collaboration and seeks faculty who can contribute to a vibrant research environment while providing exceptional educational experiences for students. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Required Qualifications : ·         Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or equivalent, ABD considered) in Kinesiology, Motor Behavior, Motor Learning, Motor Control, Neuroscience, Exercise Science, Rehabilitation Science, or a closely related field. ·         Demonstrated expertise in motor learning, motor control, motor behavior, skill acquisition, neuromotor function, or related areas. ·         Evidence of scholarly productivity commensurate with career stage, including peer-reviewed publications. ·         Demonstrated potential to develop and sustain an externally funded research program. ·         Demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate teaching. ·         Commitment to mentoring students through research, advising, and professional development. Preferred Qualifications : ·         Postdoctoral or equivalent research experience. ·         Evidence of successful or emerging external funding. ·         Research expertise in areas such as: -          Motor learning and skill acquisition -          Neuromotor rehabilitation -          Motor function across the lifespan -          Adapted physical activity and recreation -          Human performance optimization -          Technology-assisted learning and rehabilitation -          Virtual reality, augmented reality, artificial intelligence, or related approaches applied to motor behavior ·         Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students. ·         Record of interdisciplinary collaboration. ·         Experience teaching motor learning, motor control, motor behavior, adapted physical activity and recreation, research methods, or related courses. Responsibilities : The successful candidate will be expected to: ·         Develop and sustain a nationally visible research program in motor learning, motor control, or motor behavior and contribute to Baylor University's continued growth as a leading Christian research university. ·         Pursue external funding from federal, foundation, and industry sources. ·         Publish scholarly work in high-quality peer-reviewed journals. ·         Teach undergraduate and graduate courses consistent with departmental needs and their area of expertise. ·         Mentor undergraduate researchers and advise graduate students. ·         Collaborate with faculty across Baylor University and external partners to enhance interdisciplinary research opportunities. ·         Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service activities. ·         Support Baylor University's mission of integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment in a caring community. Candidates must submit all materials by October 17, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Applications will not be accepted after November 20, 2026. This search is being conducted using Interfolio’s Faculty Search platform. Applicants must submit: 1.      Formal cover letter of application addressing qualifications and research/teaching interests. 2.      Current curriculum vitae. 3.      Copy of official or unofficial transcript for highest degree. 4.      Contact information for three professional references. 5.      Completed HHPR Applicant Information Form. 6.      Self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form. Inquiries regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Andrew Meyer, at Andrew_Meyer@baylor.edu . Finalists will be invited for interviews with departmental and university leadership. All materials must be submitted via Interfolio at apply.interfolio.com/192552 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/148062": {
      "title": "Lecturers, Part-Time Temporary, Human Sciences and Design",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Human Sciences and Design Location: Waco, TX Part-time Lecturer (adjunct) positions for the Department of Human Sciences and Design, within Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences.  These positions will teach course(s) for the Department of Human Sciences and Design. With a main campus located in Waco , Texas, Baylor University is the oldest college in Texas. With a population of 21,000 diverse students, Baylor is one of the top universities in the nation, having been named an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor is also on the honor roll of the \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education; Baylor offers competitive salaries and benefits while allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest- growing parts of the state. Our strategic plan guides the University as we continue to live up to Baylor's mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. A masters degree in related field. Materials should be submitted via Interfolio"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189871": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Non-Tenure-Track, Marriage and Family Therapy",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Human Sciences and Design Location: Remote The Department of Human Sciences and Design invites applications for a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure-track core faculty position at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor to join our dynamic and collaborative Marriage and Family Therapy (MFT) faculty. The expected start date is June 1, 2027. Baylor University’s MFT program is a newly developed hybrid MS program. We are seeking an innovative faculty member who will help advance our mission to educate men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. As a hybrid program, MFT faculty and staff live across the United States. Faculty may reside remotely but are required to travel to Waco, TX periodically for designated work periods, including some weekends. As part of the Baylor family, eligible employees receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision insurance, generous time off, tuition remission, and outstanding automatic retirement contributions. To the extent that a faculty or staff member is benefits eligible, Baylor has a comprehensive benefits plan that supports you and your family’s wellbeing and allows you to be a part of the life of a vibrant and active college campus. To learn more, go to Baylor Benefits & Advantages . The budgeted salary range that the University reasonably expects to pay for this position is $ 86,000.00 - $ 96,000.00. This range takes into account the wide range of factors that are considered in making compensation decisions including but not limited to experience, skills, knowledge, abilities, education, licensure and certification, analysis of internal equity, and other business and organizational needs. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will contribute to the year-round responsibilities of teaching graduate-level MFT courses, providing clinical supervision to MFT students, coordinating offsite clinical placements, and supporting the development and implementation of clinical policies and procedures. Additional responsibilities include active participation in MFT program development, such as supporting program goals and outcomes, overseeing student capstone projects, and engaging in faculty meetings and program retreats. The candidate will also assist with accreditation activities, recruitment efforts, and applicant interviews, as well as serve on departmental, college, and university committees as required. The candidate must be able to work effectively in a team-oriented clinical environment; contribute to outreach and service initiatives; provide graduate student advising; support curriculum and program development; and fulfill other duties as assigned by the Department Chair. About Robbins College The Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences at Baylor University seeks to prepare leaders in health and quality of life through science, scholarship and innovation. Together, the departments housed within the Robbins College – Communication Sciences and Disorders; Health, Human Performance and Recreation; Human Sciences and Design; Occupational Therapy; Physical Therapy; Public Health; and a number of Army-Baylor graduate programs – promote a team-based approach to transformational education and research, establishing interdisciplinary research collaborations to advance solutions for improving quality of life for individuals, families and communities. For more information, visit the Robbins College website . Candidates  who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H1-B petition. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community . EEO/M/F/Vets/Disabled Required : Terminal degree in Marriage and Family Therapy; ABD doctoral candidates may be considered. Licensure (or eligibility for licensure) as a Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT). AAMFT Approved Supervisor Candidate. Applicants must exhibit a collaborative working style (strong communication and interpersonal skills) with faculty and students and model a philosophy consistent with the MFT Program’s vision, mission, and values, and Baylor University’s Christian mission. Preferred : Doctoral degree in Marriage and Family Therapy. Previous MFT program teaching experience and supervision within an accredited MFT program and/or with hybrid/online teaching experience preferred; 3-5 years of clinical experience and practice preferred. Previous experience in academic strategic planning, curriculum development, faculty and student recruitment and retention, program assessment, accreditation processes, clinical supervision, and offsite placement management. AAMFT Approved Supervisor. Demonstrated active involvement within professional activities at local, state, and/or national levels. APPLICATION PROCEDURE: Applicants must submit all required materials via Interfolio. A complete application includes the following: Letter of application that specifically addresses how your qualifications align with the position and how you can fulfill the stated responsibilities. A curriculum vitae. Personal teaching statement/philosophy The names and contact information of three professional references; the committee will contact references as needed. Transcript (official or unofficial) of terminal degree(s) or in progress Self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form in Interfolio--you will be asked to indicate your denominational affiliation and provide a description of your activities and involvement with your current congregation or synagogue. Review of applications will begin after October 23, 2026 at 11:59 PM Central Time. Applications MUST be submitted online by going to: https://apply.interfolio.com/ . Inquiries regarding the position may be directed to Matt Brosi at Matt_Brosi@baylor.edu. To learn more about the above position, visit Baylor Human Resources , the Child and Family Studies , and the Robbins College of Health & Human Sciences online."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189879": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Non-Tenure-Track, Architecture",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Human Sciences and Design Location: Remote The Department of Human Sciences and Design at Baylor University invites applications for a full-time, fully remote Clinical Assistant Professor in Architecture to teach in its inaugural Master of Architecture (M.Arch) program. We seek a candidate who is dedicated to innovative teaching, program development, and meaningful student engagement. As a Christian university, Baylor seeks faculty who have an active Christian or Jewish faith and who will support its mission by fostering academic excellence within a caring, faith-informed community. The successful candidate will demonstrate expertise in design, with an active role in shaping the program. This position is responsible for developing and teaching design studios and core lecture courses, such as graduate-level design studio, site and programming, building systems, portfolio workshops, and electives on a rotating basis. In addition, the faculty member will support academic services, program accreditation, as well as other efforts to help shape and grow the program. This is a remote position. It is a renewable, non-tenure-track, full-time, 12-month, and teaching-focused role. Because the M.Arch program is delivered in a hybrid format, periodic travel to Waco, TX, is required for designated in-person activities, including program Immersions and course development. As part of the Baylor family, eligible employees receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision insurance, generous time off, tuition remission, and outstanding automatic retirement contributions. To the extent that a faculty or staff member is benefits eligible, Baylor has a comprehensive benefits plan that supports you and your family’s wellbeing and allows you to be a part of the life of a vibrant and active college campus. To learn more, go to Baylor Benefits & Advantages . The budgeted salary range that the University reasonably expects to pay for this position is $ 88,000 - 98,000. This range takes into account the wide range of factors that are considered in making compensation decisions including but not limited to experience, skills, knowledge, abilities, education, licensure and certification, analysis of internal equity, and other business and organizational needs. The anticipated start date for this position is June 2027. Duties and Responsibilities •          Teach graduate architecture design studios and relevant lecture courses including: site and programming, building systems, electives, and portfolio workshops •          Support course development and program accreditation processes •          Engage with student advising and admission processes within the M.Arch program About Robbins College The Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences at Baylor University seeks to prepare leaders in health and quality of life through science, scholarship and innovation. Together, the departments housed within the Robbins College – Communication Sciences and Disorders; Health, Human Performance and Recreation; Human Sciences and Design; Occupational Therapy; Physical Therapy; Public Health; and a number of Army-Baylor graduate programs – promote a team-based approach to transformational education and research, establishing interdisciplinary research collaborations to advance solutions for improving quality of life for individuals, families and communities. For more information, visit the Robbins College website . About Baylor University Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as one of the top universities in the nation, achieving R1 institution status by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor also made it to the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education . It offers competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Required qualifications: •          Terminal professional degree in the field (ex. Master of Architecture or international equivalent) •          Demonstrated ability to teach design studio and related courses in a professional degree program •          Hold an active Christian or Jewish faith and will support Baylor’s mission within a faith-based community Preferred qualifications: •          Professional practice experience that demonstrates outstanding design skills and excellence in design work •          Experience teaching in a hybrid or online capacity •          Professional Architectural licensure Review of applications will begin October 12. Nothing received after November 30, 2026 can be considered. Applicants must submit required materials through Interfolio, which include the following: 1.       Letter of application that specifically addresses how your qualifications align with the position and how you can fulfill the stated responsibilities. 2.       Curriculum vitae 3.       Teaching Portfolio that demonstrates past student design work; under 40 MB 4.       Unofficial transcripts of terminal degree(s) 5.       Contact information for three references 6.       Self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form in Interfolio--you will be asked to indicate your denominational affiliation and provide a description of your activities and involvement with your current congregation or synagogue For questions regarding the application process or the position, contact Yoonjee Koh, Search Committee Chair, at yoonjee_koh@baylor.edu Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188204": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Part-Time Temporary, Occupational Therapy Department, Spring/Summer 2027",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Occupational Therapy Location: Waco, TX and/or Remote Adjunct Faculty Role: Adjunct Faculty are essential for curricular delivery in the Baylor Occupational Therapy Program(s). This is primarily achieved during onsite lab immersions but may also be conducted via synchronous or asynchronous lectures. Each adjunct brings essential knowledge, skills, and abilities of contemporary expertise to their course(s). Adjunct Faculty demonstrate competence in teaching and implementing strategies for student success by delivering assigned courses/objectives in a manner that facilitates student learning and mastery of course material. Primary Functions: Teaching is the primary responsibility of Adjunct Faculty. The functions of adjunct faculty may include some or all of the following, depending on the terms and conditions of their appointment: Meet deadlines and follow directions of the lead course instructor(s), Program and Department leadership, and the Dean/Associate Dean of the College. Demonstrate a command of the discipline and skill in presenting it effectively in the context of an integrated education. Maintain accurate and complete records on student participation and performance, use appropriate measures and evaluate student performance based on established student learning outcomes, provide timely feedback to students, and assign grades that are an accurate and fair evaluation of student work. Submit grades and any other required documentation in a timely manner. Teach assigned courses and tasks in accordance with the Program’s approved course description and competency-based student learning outcomes. Incorporate appropriate teaching-learning strategies, technologies, and assessment methods for evaluation of student learning into the course. Integrate information literacy and writing into courses as appropriate. Collaborate with the appropriate Core Faculty and the Program Director to identify and address student issues as appropriate. Adhere to professional and ethical standards of conduct. Maintain current professional certification and licensure requirements within the specific discipline. Maintain professional practice knowledge base and clinical expertise needed to help learners prepare for contemporary occupational therapy practice. Use current research findings and scholarly works in Occupational therapy to improve Occupational therapy education and practice. Promote professionalism by modeling and encouraging professional behaviors inside and outside the educational setting. Assist in all course related activities and complete other duties as assigned by the lead course instructor(s). Secondary Functions: These expectations do not apply to all adjunct faculty positions: Plan and deliver individual classes via distance education or face-to-face lab instruction that conform to the syllabus and other requirements of the University. Develop a syllabus of course activities that meet the requirements of the course description or program chair, establish appropriate student learning outcomes, and provide for appropriate class activities throughout the semester. Participate in course, curriculum, and program assessment activities. Meet all scheduled classes and adhere to the academic schedule, which includes final exam times and other program-related testing. As part of the Baylor family, eligible employees receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision insurance, generous time off, tuition remission, and outstanding automatic retirement contributions.  To the extent that a faculty or staff member is benefits eligible, Baylor has a comprehensive benefits plan that supports you and your family's well-being and allows you to be a part of the life of a vibrant and active college campus.  To learn more, go to Baylor Benefits & Advantages . Compensation: The budgeted salary the University reasonably expects to pay for the lab adjunct position is $75.00 per lab contact hour. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas, and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as one of the top universities in the nation, achieving R1 institution status by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor also made it to the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education . It offers competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Minimum: Occupational Therapy or Occupational Therapy Assistant license in good standing. Licensed Occupational Therapist with a master’s degree from an accredited institution with appropriate advanced practice experience will be considered for this position. Texas Occupational Therapy license in good standing. Must have at least applied for a Texas license, if not already obtained, before December 19, 2026. Preferred: Doctoral degree or its equivalent in the appropriate discipline from an accredited institution. Current certification as an OTR or COTA. Additional Skills: Exhibited evidence of continued professional growth and development. Demonstrated commitment to using innovative instructional techniques and technologies and course management systems. Application must include a curriculum vitae, official transcripts, and a copy of your OT license. Electronic (PDF) copies of all application materials are required. Completed self-disclosed Part-Time Mission Review Completed course availability form For full consideration for: Spring/Summer Trimester apply by August 31, 2026 Hiring Timeline: October 2026 – Spring/Summer Hires Selected"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187705": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Part-Time Temporary, Public Health 2027",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Health and Human Sciences: HHS Buffer: Public Health Location: Waco, TX (on campus) Part-time Lecturer (adjunct) positions for the Department of Public Health, within the Robbins College of Health and Human Sciences. These positions will teach course(s) for the Department of Public Health. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as one of the top universities in the nation, achieving R1 institution status by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor also made it to the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education . It offers competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Applicants must have completed a master’s degree in public health and/or a field related to the specific courses hired to teach. University teaching and online teaching experience is strongly preferred. Applicants whose philosophy is compatible with Baylor’s Christian mission will be considered: Baylor's Christian mission: https://www.baylor.edu/about/index.php?id=88781 Baylor's vision & strategic plan: https://strategicplan.web.baylor.edu/download Applicants must submit an initial application packet that contains: (1) a formal letter of application specifically addressing how you meet course-specific teaching qualifications and can fulfill responsibilities, (2) a full curriculum vitae or resume, (3) an unofficial transcript of the highest degree earned (master’s or doctoral), and (4) three references including names, titles, and all contact information. (Place each reference in a separate document to upload individually.) All materials must be submitted as PDF (portable document format) files in the Interfolio system. Applicants must also complete a Part-Time Mission Review form."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189454": {
      "title": "Lecturers, Part-Time, Temporary, Educational Leadership (AY 2026-2027)",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Education: EDU Buffer: Educational Leadership Location: Waco, Texas The department of Educational Leadership is seeking temporary, part-time lecturers to teach available courses in their various programs. SCHOOL: For more than 100 years, the School of Education has advanced Baylor University’s mission across the globe while preparing students for a range of careers focused on education, leadership, and human development. With more than 60 full-time faculty members, the school’s growing research and outreach portfolio complements its long-standing commitment to excellence in teaching and mentorship. Baylor School of Education’s undergraduate teacher education programs have earned national distinction for innovative partnerships with local schools that provide future educators with deep clinical preparation. Likewise, the school’s graduate programs have attained national recognition for their exemplary preparation of research scholars, educational leaders, innovators, and clinicians. Visit www.baylor.edu/SOE to learn more. About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as one of the top universities in the nation, achieving R1 institution status by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor also made it to the honor roll of \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education . It offers competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Consistent with Baylor University’s stated mission to be a world-class institution dedicated to Christian principles and ideals, the qualifications for the position include: An advanced degree in Educational Leadership or a related discipline. Evidence of excellence in teaching at the university level. Candidates should include the following in their application materials: (a) completed application form, (b) a curriculum vitae, and (c) transcripts documenting the terminal degree. All applicants must complete the self-disclosed Part-Time Mission Review in Interfolio."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185023": {
      "title": "Lecturers, Part-Time, Temporary, Educational Psychology",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Education: EDU Buffer: Educational Psychology Location: Waco, Texas The department of Educational Psychology is seeking temporary, part-time lecturers to teach available courses in their various programs. SCHOOL: For more than 100 years, the School of Education has advanced Baylor University’s mission across the globe while preparing students for a range of careers focused on education, leadership, and human development. With more than 60 full-time faculty members, the school’s growing research and outreach portfolio complements its long-standing commitment to excellence in teaching and mentorship. Baylor School of Education’s undergraduate teacher education programs have earned national distinction for innovative partnerships with local schools that provide future educators with deep clinical preparation. Likewise, the school’s graduate programs have attained national recognition for their exemplary preparation of research scholars, educational leaders, innovators, and clinicians. Visit www.baylor.edu/SOE to learn more. About Baylor University: Located in Waco, Texas , Baylor University is the oldest college in Texas. With a population of 21,000 diverse students, Baylor is one of the top universities in the nation, having been named an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification in January 2022. Baylor is also on the honor roll of the \"Great Colleges to Work For\" from The Chronicle of Higher Education ; Baylor offers competitive salaries and benefits while allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. Our strategic plan, Illuminate , guides the University as we continue to live up to Baylor's mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Consistent with Baylor University’s stated mission to be a world-class institution dedicated to Christian principles and ideals, the qualifications for the position include: An advanced degree in Educational Psychology or a related discipline. Evidence of excellence in teaching at the university level. Candidates should include the following in their application materials: (a) completed application form, (b) a curriculum vitae, and (c) transcripts documenting the terminal degree. All applicants must complete the self-disclosed Part-Time Mission Review in Interfolio."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190574": {
      "title": "Patterson Endowed Chair of Cybersecurity and Professor, Tenured, Computer Science",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Engineering and Computer Science: ECS Buffer: Computer Science Location: Waco, TX The Department of Computer Science at Baylor University seeks qualified candidates for the Patterson Endowed Chair position in Cybersecurity .  This tenured professor position will begin in August 2027. We look for exceptional candidates with vision who will expand innovative research and teaching that addresses challenging problems in the field of cybersecurity.  Applications from all areas within cybersecurity are encouraged. The candidate will have exceptional international research credentials in cybersecurity, a strong track record of securing research funding, and experience leading research initiatives. Excellence in teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels is essential. This pivotal role calls for an established leader who will forge and drive research collaborations inside the department or across the university. Baylor University’s Cybersecurity Research and Education Initiative aims to significantly advance knowledge within the cybersecurity community. Baylor is designated by the National Security Agency (NSA) as a National Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education (CAE-CD) and Cyber Research (CAE-R). Additionally, the Central Texas Cyber Range (CTCR) equipped with state-of-the-art facilities fosters cybersecurity education, applied research, and community engagement. About the Department: Baylor’s ABET-accredited Computer Science Department currently has twelve tenured/tenure-track faculty, including the McCollum Family Chair of Data Science, and seven lecturer faculty members. The faculty are internationally recognized in research areas including data science, bioinformatics, machine learning, cybersecurity, computer vision, and computer systems. The department is housed within the Hankamer Building and the Baylor Research and Innovation Collaborative (BRIC; see https://bric.research.baylor.edu/ ). The department offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees in Computer Science. It also offers the BSI degree with majors in Bioinformatics, Data Science, and Cybersecurity. Additional information regarding the department, including its mission, is available at https://www.ecs.baylor.edu/research-departments/computer-science . About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Distinguishing Expectations of the Patterson Endowed Chair The holder of the Patterson Endowed Chair will be expected to: Serve as a visible ambassador for Baylor University nationally and internationally. Lead transformative research initiatives aligned with instructional priorities. Assist in recruiting outstanding faculty, graduate students, and postdoctoral scholars. Forster interdisciplinary collaborations across the university. Advance Baylor’s visibility among federal sponsors and industry partners. Contribute to the development of future research centers and strategic initiatives. Qualifications Education & Experience : A Ph.D. in cybersecurity, or a closely related field, along with a minimum of 10 years of professional experience post Ph.D. degree. Research Leadership & Center Creation : A proven track record of visionary leadership. Strong preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated success in leading major research initiatives, centers, institutes, laboratories, or large-scale collaborative programs involving multiple investigators, institutions, and external stakeholders.  Experience securing substantial federal, industrial, or foundation support is highly desired. Scholarly Excellence : A distinguished record of high-impact scholarship, including nationally or internationally recognized publications and a strong history of securing significant external research funding. Teaching & Mentorship : Demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring students, postdoctoral scholars, and early-career faculty.  A strong record of graduate student placement, research mentorship, and talent development is highly desirable. National and International Recognition : Evidence of national or international leadership in the field through major awards, fellow status in professional societies, editorial responsibilities, invited keynote presentations, professional service, or other indicators of scholarly distinction. Partnership Development : Demonstrated ability to cultivate productive partnerships with federal agencies, industry, national laboratories, healthcare organizations, nonprofits, or other external stakeholders that enhance research impact and educational opportunities. Evaluation Criteria Research Excellence Scholarly impact and reputation Research vision and innovation Record of external funding Potential for center or institute leadership Academic Leadership Strategic leadership Faculty mentorship Interdisciplinary collaboration Programmatic development Educational Impact Teaching effectiveness Graduate mentoring Student success outcomes Institutional Fit Ability to advance Baylor’s mission Communication and collegiality Commitment to Christian higher education Required Documents: - Cover letter - CV (Curriculum Vitae) - Statement of research interests - Statement of teaching interests - Contact information for at least three professional references - Academic transcript of highest degree earned (unofficial is accepted) - Religious Affiliation Form (available in Interfolio) Optional Documents: - Publications Review of applicants will begin on October 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Nothing received after December 31, 2026 can be considered. All applicants will also complete the self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form (RAF) in Interfolio. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Greg Speegle at “Greg_Speegle@baylor.edu”. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191026": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Computer Science – Cybersecurity",
      "description": "Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Engineering and Computer Science: ECS Buffer: Computer Science Location: Waco, TX The Department of Computer Science at Baylor University seeks qualified candidates for a tenure-track position with the rank of Assistant Professor in Cybersecurity .  This position will begin in August 2027. Successful candidates must have a Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related discipline. We seek exceptional candidates in broad areas of cybersecurity. Applications from all areas within Cybersecurity are encouraged. Potential topics include but are not limited to foundations for information security (cryptography and formal methods), system security (hardware, software, platforms) across a wide range of systems, network and wireless security, AI security, human factors in security, and privacy. Successful candidates will have a commitment to excellence in teaching, exhibit the potential to support an independent research agenda, and have effective communication and organization skills. Baylor University’s Cybersecurity Research and Education Initiative aims to significantly advance knowledge within the cybersecurity community. Baylor is designated by the National Security Agency (NSA) as a National Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education (CAE-CD) and Cyber Research (CAE-R). Additionally, the Central Texas Cyber Range (CTCR) equipped with state-of-the-art facilities fosters cybersecurity education, applied research, and community engagement. The selected candidate will be expected to initiate and conduct research as well as perform academic duties associated with our undergraduate and graduate programs. The primary responsibilities are teaching courses, developing an externally funded research program, and leading graduate and undergraduate students in research. Active participation in departmental service is also expected. About the Department: Baylor’s ABET-accredited Computer Science Department currently has twelve tenured/tenure-track faculty, including the McCollum Family Chair of Data Science, and seven lecturer faculty members. The faculty are internationally recognized in research areas including data science, bioinformatics, machine learning, cybersecurity, computer vision, and computer systems. The department is housed within the Hankamer Building and the Baylor Research and Innovation Collaborative (BRIC; see https://bric.research.baylor.edu/ ). The department offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees in Computer Science. It also offers the BSI degree with majors in Bioinformatics, Data Science, and Cybersecurity. Additional information regarding the department, including its mission, is available at https://www.ecs.baylor.edu/research-departments/computer-science . About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Required qualifications: A Ph.D. in Computer Science, or a closely related field is required. A commitment to teaching excellence in areas relevant to the position and, for candidates with prior teaching experience, a record of successful teaching A demonstrated research achievement and publication record commensurate with appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor Outstanding communication skills Preferred qualifications: Special consideration will be given to candidates who have demonstrated strong scholarship and have an established and active independent research agenda in cybersecurity or closely related areas. To exhibit a passion for teaching and mentoring at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Please provide the following documents through Interfolio: Cover letter, which includes the applicant’s anticipated rank CV (Curriculum Vitae) Statement of research interests Statement of teaching interests related to Baylor's programs Contact information for at least three professional references Academic transcript of highest degree earned (Unofficial is accepted) Religious Affiliation Form (found in Interfolio) The following documents are optional: Publications Review of applicants will begin on October 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Nothing received after December 31, 2026 can be considered. All applicants will also complete the self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form (RAF) in Interfolio. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Greg Speegle at “Greg_Speegle@baylor.edu”. Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191028": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Tenure Track or Tenured, Computer Science - Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Posted: Aug 21, 2026 Deadline: Dec 31, 2026 Department: Baylor University: Office of the Provost: Engineering and Computer Science: ECS Buffer: Computer Science Location: Waco, Texas The Department of Computer Science at Baylor University seeks qualified candidates for two tenure-track or tenured positions with the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in Artificial Intelligence (AI) .  This position will begin in August 2027. Successful candidates must have a Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related discipline. We seek exceptional candidates in broad areas of artificial intelligence, data science, and machine learning. Successful candidates will have a commitment to excellence in research and teaching, exhibit the potential to support an independent research agenda, and have effective communication and organization skills. The selected candidate will be expected to initiate and conduct research as well as perform academic duties associated with our undergraduate and graduate programs. The primary responsibilities are developing an externally funded research program, teaching courses, and leading graduate and undergraduate students in research. Active participation in departmental service is also expected. Baylor’s ABET-accredited Computer Science Department currently has twelve tenured/tenure-track faculty, including the McCollum Family Chair of Data Science, and seven lecturer faculty members. The faculty are internationally recognized in research areas including data science, bioinformatics, machine learning, cybersecurity, computer vision, and computer systems. The department is housed within the Hankamer Building and the Baylor Research and Innovation Collaborative (BRIC; see https://bric.research.baylor.edu/ ). The department offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees in Computer Science. It also offers the BSI degree with majors in Bioinformatics, Data Science, and Cybersecurity. Additional information regarding the department, including its mission, is available at https://www.ecs.baylor.edu/research-departments/computer-science . About Baylor University: Baylor University is located in Waco, Texas and is the oldest college in the state. It has a diverse student population of 21,000 and is recognized as an R1 institution by the Carnegie Classification. Baylor is also noted on the honor roll of “Great Colleges to Work For” by ModernThink. We offer competitive salaries and benefits , allowing faculty and staff to live in one of the fastest-growing parts of the state. As a Christian university with historic Baptist roots and as reflected in the Notice of Non-Discrimination , Baylor strives to be a place characterized by civility and respect. We believe each student, faculty, staff, and administrator is made in the image of God. Baylor's new strategic plan, Baylor in Deeds , guides the University as it continues to fulfill its mission of educating men and women for worldwide leadership and service by integrating academic excellence and Christian commitment within a caring community. Required qualifications: A Ph.D. in Computer Science, or a closely related field is required. A commitment to teaching excellence in areas relevant to the position and, for candidates with prior teaching experience, a record of successful teaching A demonstrated research achievement and publication record commensurate with appointment at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor Outstanding communication skills Preferred qualifications: Special consideration will be given to candidates who have demonstrated strong scholarship and have an established and active independent research agenda in artificial intelligence or closely related areas. To exhibit a passion for teaching and mentoring at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Qualities of a successful candidate for a senior position include leadership experience. Please provide the following documents through Interfolio: Cover letter, which includes the applicant’s anticipated rank CV (Curriculum Vitae) Statement of research interests Statement of teaching interests related to Baylor's programs Contact information for at least three professional references Academic transcript of highest degree earned (Unofficial is accepted) Religious Affiliation Form (found in Interfolio) The following documents are optional: Publications Candidates who are outside of the United States and do not have other nonimmigrant visa status will not be sponsored for an H-1B petition. Review of applicants will begin on October 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Nothing received after December 31, 2026 can be considered. All applicants will also complete the self-disclosed Religious Affiliation Form (RAF) in Interfolio."
